                    {
                        "translation_id": "761dcc7e-bc28-436f-8a6a-67af1b9100dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "5be2ec0e-7354-38b9-8dcd-97a5c86ed22b",
                        "source_sense_id": "dc977080-3902-3b58-97b0-537463a460bd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zustand oder Eigenschaft, langweilig, fade oder geschmacklos zu sein",
                        "target_lang_word": "blandness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blandness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec5788f-75d4-34ac-bf5a-e1261cc5238c",
                                        "entry_id": "c9f60c09-ca7b-3720-906f-8f876aef36c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state, quality, or characteristic of being bland.",
                                            "Mildness, gentleness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05c2edfb-47ac-4229-b71d-ff6ebf62df55",
                                                "sense_id": "aec5788f-75d4-34ac-bf5a-e1261cc5238c",
                                                "text": "These temporary apprehensions, so vague but so awful, derived a wondrous potency from the contrasting serenity of the weather, in which, beneath all its blue blandness, some thought there lurked a devilish charm, as for days and days we voyaged along, through seas so wearily, lonesomely mild, that all space, in repugnance to our vengeful errand, seemed vacating itself of life before our urn-like prow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd2c0ca6-5d56-3f66-b81c-8a2eddc7f572",
                                        "entry_id": "c9f60c09-ca7b-3720-906f-8f876aef36c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state, quality, or characteristic of being bland.",
                                            "Lack of taste or flavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21347354-9036-3357-899b-335fe9382dfb",
                                        "entry_id": "c9f60c09-ca7b-3720-906f-8f876aef36c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state, quality, or characteristic of being bland.",
                                            "Lack of interest or appeal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9b236e7-8b59-4150-b4ee-9210bede2210",
                                                "sense_id": "21347354-9036-3357-899b-335fe9382dfb",
                                                "text": "But generally, these summits have been real snoozers, producing statements of such vague blandness that they make G-20 resolutions read like Harry Potter page-turners."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cbeb4583-96d5-4142-8236-97b12555323d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5be2ec0e-7354-38b9-8dcd-97a5c86ed22b",
                        "source_sense_id": "dc977080-3902-3b58-97b0-537463a460bd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zustand oder Eigenschaft, langweilig, fade oder geschmacklos zu sein",
                        "target_lang_word": "tediousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tediousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0408a438-2e6b-3832-8de1-eac5662aa4a9",
                                        "entry_id": "bf3ee45e-c060-326b-9d9e-6fa4375a3c8f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being tedious; tedium."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e814aa82-e53d-4a33-a62a-3aca49cef3e8",
                                                "sense_id": "0408a438-2e6b-3832-8de1-eac5662aa4a9",
                                                "text": "[B]revity is the soul of wit,\nAnd tediousness the limbs and outward flourishes[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54d3dbf9-d713-4ca6-8b51-ccac0affa9c4",
                                                "sense_id": "0408a438-2e6b-3832-8de1-eac5662aa4a9",
                                                "text": "I am the worst person in the world for formal dinners, but I shall be thankful to have a resting-place whereon to bestow my tediousness in an evening."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40172913-117a-4dcb-a27b-489a4f6efd2f",
                        "source_entry_id": "5be2ec0e-7354-38b9-8dcd-97a5c86ed22b",
                        "source_sense_id": "dc977080-3902-3b58-97b0-537463a460bd",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zustand oder Eigenschaft, langweilig, fade oder geschmacklos zu sein",
                        "target_lang_word": "insipidity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "insipidity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2c33e9f-18da-3b97-b83d-60029efa3891",
                                        "entry_id": "0eb748b5-b538-38bd-8e68-aaf8476f2f01",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being insipid; insipidness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a44182e1-f60e-4824-98e8-9d13c6ee6a37",
                                                "sense_id": "a2c33e9f-18da-3b97-b83d-60029efa3891",
                                                "text": "1735, Alexander Pope, The Dunciad, Book I, Notes Variorum, in The Works of Mr. Alexander Pope, Volume 2, London: Lawton Gilliver, p. 98,\nNahum Tate was Poet Laureate, a cold writer, of no invention, but sometimes translated tolerably when befriended by Mr. Dryden. In his second part of Absalom and Achitophel are above two hundred admirable lines together of that great hand, which strongly shine through the insipidity of the rest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eeaa3b5-28f9-41d1-907c-bcb9171013f2",
                                                "sense_id": "a2c33e9f-18da-3b97-b83d-60029efa3891",
                                                "text": "Her complexion was sallow; and her features small, without beauty, and naturally without expression; but a lucky contraction of the brow had rescued her countenance from the disgrace of insipidity, by giving it the strong characters of pride and ill nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45d14667-add1-3dab-be51-ac842e5af10d",
                                        "entry_id": "0eb748b5-b538-38bd-8e68-aaf8476f2f01",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is insipid; an insipid utterance, sight, object, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b79f8f27-3428-487b-9bd4-fa2ee6a6b2a4",
                                                "sense_id": "45d14667-add1-3dab-be51-ac842e5af10d",
                                                "text": "The lovers of beauty, preferring what is dull to what is offensive, will rather doze over the inanities and insipidities of a drowsy dilettantism, than choose to be irritated into wakeful attention by ugly contours, disproportioned figures, and ill-assorted colours, drawn and arranged after the hard and ignorant manner of the early Christian painters, and imbued with the childish symbolism of the dismal Middle Ages."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73927735-63fe-4516-8ff1-c32981d09c62",
                                                "sense_id": "45d14667-add1-3dab-be51-ac842e5af10d",
                                                "text": "[…] Gilbert literally educated the English public away from the popular insipidities to which they had grown accustomed, up to a standard of taste to which all future writers of operetta must aspire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
